From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lavfi/rkrga: clear the whole crop rectangle on the output
 frame

The output frame takes its properties from the input with
av_frame_copy_props(), which copies crop_top, crop_bottom, crop_left and
crop_right. The RGA has already read the input through its crop rectangle
by then, so those fields describe a crop that has been applied; leaving
them on the output asks the next filter or the encoder to apply it again.

Only crop_top was cleared. Clear all four.

In today's pipeline the field that actually leaks is crop_left:
av_frame_apply_cropping() folds crop_right and crop_bottom into width and
height for hardware pixel formats and zeroes them before a filter ever sees
the frame. That is a property of the producer, though, not of this filter --
a caller that sets avctx->apply_cropping = 0 delivers all four intact.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavfilter/rkrga_common.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c b/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c
index 1ca7d39..79fce45 100644
--- a/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c
+++ b/libavfilter/rkrga_common.c
@@ -581,7 +581,17 @@ static RGAFrame *query_frame(RKRGAContext *r, AVFilterLink *outlink,
         av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Failed to copy metadata fields from in to out: %d\n", ret);
         goto fail;
     }
-    out_frame->frame->crop_top = 0;
+    /* The RGA has already read the input through its crop rectangle, so the
+     * output holds cropped pixels and inherited crop fields would ask a
+     * downstream filter or encoder to crop a second time. av_frame_copy_props()
+     * copies all four, so all four are cleared. Only crop_left survives to here
+     * in practice -- avcodec folds crop_right/crop_bottom into width/height for
+     * hardware formats and this function already cleared crop_top -- but that is
+     * a property of the current producer, not of this filter's contract. */
+    out_frame->frame->crop_top    = 0;
+    out_frame->frame->crop_bottom = 0;
+    out_frame->frame->crop_left   = 0;
+    out_frame->frame->crop_right  = 0;
     if (r->out_reset_sar) {
         out_frame->frame->sample_aspect_ratio = (AVRational){1, 1};
     } else if ((in0_info->rotate_mode & 0x04) == 0x04 /* HAL_TRANSFORM_ROT_90 */ ||
